"""Publish measured early-industrial calibration, including limitations and ledgers."""
import json,html
import refine_fixed_prices as s

def main():
    chosen=json.loads((s.OUT/'selected.json').read_text())
    summaries=json.loads((s.OUT/'summary.json').read_text())
    baseline=next(r for r in summaries if r['id']=='f00')
    trials=json.loads((s.OUT/'coarse-results.json').read_text())+json.loads((s.OUT/'challenge-results.json').read_text())
    data=json.dumps(dict(chosen=chosen,baseline=baseline)).replace('</','<\\/')
    rows=''
    for n,r in sorted(chosen['best'].items(),key=lambda x:int(x[0])):
        b=baseline['times'][n];t=r['result']['seconds']/60
        rows+=f'<tr><td>{n}</td><td>{r["result"]["iron"]} / {r["result"]["copper"]}</td><td>{b:.1f}</td><td><b>{t:.1f}</b></td><td>{t-b:+.1f}</td><td>{r["result"]["researchSeconds"]/60:.1f}</td></tr>'
    mid=min(chosen['times'][str(n)] for n in [4,5,6])
    page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Early industrial balance refinement</title>
<style>:root{color-scheme:dark}body{font:16px system-ui;background:#10191d;color:#e5eeeb;max-width:1120px;margin:32px auto;padding:20px}a{color:#9ddacc}p{line-height:1.6;color:#becfcb}h1{font-size:36px}.cards{display:flex;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap}.card,section{background:#1a292e;border:1px solid #38534e;border-radius:10px;padding:20px;margin:18px 0}.card{flex:1}.big{font-size:30px;color:#9ddacc}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}td,th{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #38534e;text-align:left}.scroll{overflow:auto;max-height:600px}select{font:inherit;padding:8px;background:#24383c;color:white}svg{width:100%;height:auto}pre{white-space:pre-wrap}</style>
<p><a href="action-search.html">← Fighter action search</a> · EXPERIMENTAL EARLY INDUSTRIAL PROFILE</p><h1>Invest, expand, then upgrade.</h1>
<p>Fixed per-building prices. No expansion surcharge or new game mechanics. These results cover the first industrial milestone, not the Fighter.</p>
<div class="cards"><div class="card">Paths 4–6, fastest<div class="big">MID min</div></div><div class="card">Path 1 / optimum<div class="big">LOW×</div></div><div class="card">Path 12 / optimum<div class="big">HIGH×</div></div></div>
<p>COUNT deterministic simulations completed (FAIL failed). Baseline and selected candidate each challenged with 568 allocations. Best tested routes under the policy below; no claim of a globally optimal build order.</p><p><b>Remaining shortfall:</b> the requested 2–3× penalty at path 12 is not achieved. This profile is an incremental improvement, not a completed match to the target curve.</p>
<section><h2>Measured completion times</h2><svg id="plot" viewBox="0 0 1000 270" role="img" aria-label="Baseline and candidate completion minutes by expansion path"></svg><p>Grey: accepted baseline. Green: selected candidate. Widths are spaced equally as categories.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Iron / copper sets</th><th>Baseline min</th><th>Candidate min</th><th>Change min</th><th>Research done min</th></tr></thead><tbody>ROWS</tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h2>What is being compared</h2><p>Path 1 starts with one iron and one copper miner–smelter–workshop set. Path N adds N−1 sets; the first addition is iron, and later additions can be iron or copper. Thus path 5 means six total metal sets, not five machines.</p><p>Empty starting inventory; already-built starter machines and 15 belt tiles. Coal miners and basic generators are bought as needed. Silica and refractory costs are omitted. Power is binary and machines can be paused. All added metal sets are replaced with industrial miners, industrial smelters, and structural/electrical specialists; generators remain basic.</p><p>Transfers are ideal manual logistics with no player effort time or throughput limit. Existing belts still consume power. This deliberately avoids creating an overexpansion penalty from a fixed belt cap; paid belt layout and capacity need a separate validation.</p><p>Purchases within each set and industrial replacements are sequential. Industrial replacement order is fixed: initial iron set, initial copper set, remaining iron sets, then copper sets. Basic and industrial machines both keep producing during the transition. Wider paths finish larger factories, so their extra time is not solely waste toward an identical endpoint.</p></section>
<section><h2>Selected parameters</h2><p>Multipliers below are relative to the original game catalog. BasicCost affects basic miners, smelters and workshops. PowerCost affects basic generator prices. Capital affects the four industrial/specialist building types. Speed affects basic/industrial miners and early processing recipes; industrialRate is an additional multiplier for industrial production. Refund is the returned fraction. Research cost is multiplied; research and construction durations stay unchanged.</p><pre>PARAMS</pre><p>The live game catalog has not been changed. The selected economy is saved as <code>reports/starter-fixed-refinement/candidate.catalog.json</code>.</p></section>
<section><h2>Build sequence and waiting</h2><label>Path <select id="route"></select></label><p>Elapsed time between milestones includes production, funding waits and construction; it is not a pure idle-time measurement.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Milestone</th><th>At minute</th><th>Since previous</th></tr></thead><tbody id="ledger"></tbody></table></div></section>
<script>const data=DATA;const chosen=data.chosen;const paths=Object.keys(chosen.best).map(Number).sort((a,b)=>a-b);const max=Math.max(...Object.values(chosen.times),...Object.values(data.baseline.times));const ns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';const plot=document.querySelector('#plot');function el(tag,attrs,text){const e=document.createElementNS(ns,tag);for(const [k,v] of Object.entries(attrs))e.setAttribute(k,v);if(text!==undefined)e.textContent=text;plot.appendChild(e)}paths.forEach((n,i)=>{const x=45+i*920/paths.length;for(const [offset,value,color] of [[0,data.baseline.times[n],'#657d80'],[17,chosen.times[n],'#9ddacc']]){const h=value/max*210;el('rect',{x:x+offset,y:230-h,width:14,height:h,fill:color})}el('text',{x:x+12,y:253,fill:'#dce8e4','text-anchor':'middle','font-size':13},n)});el('text',{x:10,y:15,fill:'#dce8e4','font-size':13},Math.ceil(max)+' min');const select=document.querySelector('#route');paths.forEach(n=>{const o=document.createElement('option');o.value=n;o.textContent=n;select.appendChild(o)});select.value=5;function render(){let prev=0;document.querySelector('#ledger').replaceChildren(...chosen.best[select.value].result.marks.map(m=>{const tr=document.createElement('tr');[m.action,(m.seconds/60).toFixed(2),((m.seconds-prev)/60).toFixed(2)].forEach(t=>{const td=document.createElement('td');td.textContent=t;tr.appendChild(td)});prev=m.seconds;return tr}))}select.onchange=render;render();</script></html>'''
    replacements={'MID':f'{mid:.1f}','LOW':f'{chosen["times"]["1"]/mid:.2f}','HIGH':f'{chosen["times"]["12"]/mid:.2f}','COUNT':str(len(trials)),'FAIL':str(sum(not r['result']['success'] for r in trials)),'ROWS':rows,'PARAMS':html.escape(json.dumps(chosen['parameters'],indent=2)),'DATA':data}
    for key,val in replacements.items():page=page.replace(key,val)
    (s.OUT/'report.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8');(s.s.HERE/'web/starter-refinement.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
    print('Published starter-refinement.html')

if __name__=='__main__':main()
